# One line per student: student id, tenant id, broker username.
#
# Passwords are NOT here. bin/provision.sh generates them, writes the broker
# users and the caddy credential files under secrets/, and leaves one connection
# sheet per student under sheets/. Both directories are gitignored.
#
# The tenant id becomes one word of an AMQP routing key, so it must match
# ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]*$ — no dots, no `*`, no `#`. provision.sh checks it, which
# is the check that rungs 1-2 of the template do not do for themselves.
#
# Student id is only ever used for file names and the access log, so make it
# something you can read at a glance in a log line at 2am.
#
# student,tenant,broker_user
alice,tenant-alice,alice
bob,tenant-bob,bob
carol,tenant-carol,carol
